Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-08-2000||09:24 PM||||    Ok, So I was thinking, what if I were to obtain a 3.1L or 3.4L long block? Exactly how easy is it to just "SWAP" out the parts<BR>of my current 2.8L? I mean, is it realy that easy? You just take the plenum, water pump, and attached engine parts and  sensors and move them to the new block? What about the ECM? Is there any tricks or mods necessary to make the fit <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> Seriously, if it's that easy, You, "THE FORUM" have probly saved me hundreds of dollars and months off my estimated time of completion <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I won't even mess with 2.8; I'll just "SWAP" it for what it would be anyway, and save myself all the technical headaches. Am I making any sense? This is what I mean when I say, I appriciate what you all do for me and my limited mechanical knowledge. This is the greatest place in net space. Anyway, if you set all kidding aside, I really am looking for the easiest, most economical way of getting that little bit of additional power that only the "ASSOMETER" can guage. Any replies and advice will be taken seriously and considered. (You probably could'nt tell I have had some Post Secondary Education). <P>Thanx To The FORUM <BR> You Guys/Gals are the best<P> BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||6
Z||000001||batboy||03-08-2000||10:43 PM||||Be careful which 3.1 engine you ask for, most of them have aluminum heads and require a different intake and ECM. The 3.1 engine you want with cast iron heads are mainly out of early 90's FWD minivans. These reman engines might have the low power heads and wimpy cam though. The Fiero 2.8 engines had the HO heads with bigger valves.||||reg||1
